When $c=1$, the loss of multi-head attention indicated by Theorem~\ref{thm:multi_head} can be reduced to the optimal loss of single-head attention:
\begin{eqnarray*}
&&L_{\text{multi}}(A_1,A_2,b_1,b_2,v)\big|_{c=1}=\frac{v^2}{D}\left(\frac{v^2}{v^2-2}\right)^\frac{d}{2} + \frac{v^2}{D(v^2-2)}\left(\frac{v^2}{v^2-2}\right)^\frac{d}{2}+o(\frac{1}{D})\approx L_{\text{sing}}(A^*,b^*,v).
    \end{eqnarray*}
Upon differentiation, we have $\frac{\partial}{\partial c} L_{\text{multi}}\left( A_1, A_2, b_1, b_2, v \right)\big|_{c=1}=0$, and 
 \begin{eqnarray*}
