(v^2-2)^3}\right)-\frac{8v^4\left(d+2\right)d}{D}\left(\frac{(\frac{v^2}{v^2-2})^{d/2}}{
(v^2-2)^4}\right)<0.
\end{eqnarray*} 
Therefore, when fixing other parameters, $c=1$ is a local maximum of the loss function, indicating that there must exist some $0<c^*<1$ such that $L_{\text{multi}}(A_1,A_2,b_1,b_2,v)\big|_{c=c^*} < L_{\text{multi}}(A_1,A_2,b_1,b_2,v)\big|_{c=1}\approx L_{\text{sing}}(A^*,b^*,v).$

